4,Daai Sa Noh Im kkit Nih Mshu Be Vai - Yang Long & Rockie ...Daai language - WikipediaDaai Chin - WikipediaStream Naing Shin | Listen to Daai Traditional Songs playlist ...Daai language — GrokipediaCentral Asia-Elements & Tibetan Music,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7romYawdUag,"Jul 21, 2025 · Daai Sa Noh Im kkit Nih Mshu Be Vai - Yang Long & Rockie Mnaai ( daai song) AI DAAI TUBE Production 680 subscribers It is spoken in 142 villages in Kanpetlet, Matupi, Mindat, and Paletwa townships in Chin State, Burma (Ethnologue). A written script for Daai was created in 1976 by U Khine Sho and Ms. Halga So Hart Manno. The Daai-Chin are of Tibeto-Burman descent. They primarily live in Mindat, Paletwa, Matupi, and Kanpetlet townships of southern Chin State. With more than 180 villages and a population estimated between 35,000 and 45,000, the Daai-Chin represent the majority ethnic group in the Southern Chin Hills. Listen to Daai Traditional Songs, a playlist curated by Naing Shin on desktop and mobile. Daai Chin, commonly referred to as Daai, is a Tibeto-Burman language belonging to the Southern Chin branch of the Kuki-Chin-Naga subgroup within the Sino-Tibetan family. A Tibetan Rul-Mo Performance audio: an invocation of Mahakala, protector deity of Tibetan Buddhism excerpt from a puja - an extended ritual of chant, instrumental music and offerings rul-mo cymbals played with a brdung (series of accelerating strikes) What language is Daai? Daai (also known as Daai Chin), which borders the Mün and Ütbü language groups, is a Kuki-Chin of Myanmar (Burma). It is spoken in 142 villages in Kanpetlet, Matupi, Mindat, and Paletwa townships in Chin State, Burma (Ethnologue). A written script for Daai was created in 1976 by U Khine Sho and Ms. Halga So Hart Manno. What is the lexical similarity of Daai Chin? Daai has greater than 90% lexical similarity with Daa Yindu, Yang, Mkui, Duk, and Msang, 81%–88% with Ngxang (Paletwa township) and Kheng, 80% with Shiip (Matupi township), 91%–94% with Gah/Ng-Gha (part of Mün), and 81%–87% with Mün. Ethnologue lists the following dialects of daai Chin. Daai has twenty-four consonant phonemes. How many Daai-speaking regions are there in Chin State? The Daai-speaking region is administratively divided into four regions within Chin State: Kanpetlet, Mindat, Matupi, and Paletwa. Each region is sometimes referred to by local names such as Kanpetlet Daai, Mindat Daai, Matu Daai, and Paletwa Daai. Is Daai a Christian or a Khuum? Their ethnic symbol is the khuum (rocket-tail dragon), and their royal flower is the ling leih (Bulbophyllum refractum, an orchid species). Today, about 99% of Daai people identify as Christians. The Daai inhabit a region in the southern part of Chin State, Myanmar, which lies within the country's western mountain zone.","Chin, Daai",Sino-Tibetan
